diff --git a/PRD.md b/PRD.md
index 179723a..f31fd30 100644
--- a/PRD.md
+++ b/PRD.md
@@ -264,7 +264,9 @@ The system may let the user import private replacement content prepared by Codex
 - Each import candidate is represented by a package containing a manifest plus one Markdown or EPUB content file. Markdown packages may also include bounded sidecar image attachments referenced by that Markdown file; EPUB packages must keep their assets inside the EPUB and may not add package sidecars.
 - The package manifest stores title, topic tags, source label, rights class, optional description, optional priority intent, and enough file identity data to detect duplicates.
 - Agent-supplied content is treated as `user_private` by default and must not become shared editorial inventory.
-- Agent-supplied priority is visible before import. The user can accept or remove the priority before saving.
+- Agent-supplied priority is visible before import. The default behavior is manual review: the user can accept or remove the priority before saving. Autoimport may auto-accept manifest `high` priority only when the user has explicitly selected an Agent Inbox priority mode that allows it. A separate ignore mode must prevent manifest priority from affecting ranking even if the manifest asks for `high`.
+- Agent Inbox import options let the user choose whether imported packages keep manifest topics or are saved without a specific category. Because the current document model requires at least one topic tag, the no-specific-category mode stores the imported document under `OTHER` rather than trusting agent-selected topical categories.
+- Settings exposes a copyable, portable agent prompt for package authoring. The prompt must not contain user-specific Drive ids, account names, rclone remotes, tokens, local absolute paths, or machine-specific assumptions, and it must require package validation before upload.
 - Invalid, unsupported, duplicated, unavailable, partially missing, or over-limit packages are visible as finite review items and are not silently imported.
 - Importing an accepted package uses the same user-document model, reading-time estimation, progress tracking, and reader behavior as manually imported Markdown or EPUB documents.
 - The Agent Inbox review surface is finite and must not become a discovery feed.
@@ -498,7 +500,7 @@ The system must provide account-like portability without requiring a Quality Alt
 - Portable profile exports must be human-auditable JSON rather than opaque database backups.
 - Export/import should preserve behaviorally important state without pretending to provide server-backed identity, cross-device conflict resolution, or guaranteed document-file transfer.
 - Any cloud sync must be explicit, revocable, and scoped to user-owned files. Cloud authorization state must be re-established on each device rather than copied through profile export.
-- Agent Inbox cloud access must remain explicit, revocable, finite, and user-reviewed by default. The product must not ingest agent-produced Drive content without a visible accept/reject step unless the user has explicitly enabled Agent Inbox autoimport for the already selected folder. Autoimport is opt-in, revocable from Settings, limited to the selected Agent Inbox folder, and must not silently accept a manifest priority request; high-priority requests affect ranking only after explicit user acceptance.
+- Agent Inbox cloud access must remain explicit, revocable, finite, and user-reviewed by default. The product must not ingest agent-produced Drive content without a visible accept/reject step unless the user has explicitly enabled Agent Inbox autoimport for the already selected folder. Autoimport is opt-in, revocable from Settings, limited to the selected Agent Inbox folder, and must not silently accept a manifest priority request unless the user has explicitly selected the auto-accept high-priority import option; high-priority requests otherwise affect ranking only after explicit user acceptance.
 - Agent Inbox Drive access must prefer user-scoped folder selection over broader Drive scopes. Android `OpenDocumentTree` is the primary user-facing selector because it gives a revocable persisted read grant to the selected folder tree without requiring a pasted Drive id. Google file Picker is not sufficient for externally populated Agent Inbox folders. Any visible `drive.readonly` path must be explicit, revocable, limited in app behavior to the selected or user-supplied Agent Inbox folder id, and described as broader Drive read authorization.
 - Website matching must remain local-first and user-authored. The app must not collect browsing history as an input or side effect of website target matching.
 
